  "body": "Part of #902. Since #902 the document's unit is the program's unit, and the Fanuc Lathe post refuses an inch document by name (`programUnits = \"mm\"` in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`).\n\nInch turning is more than dividing lengths by 25.4: G96 S is surface feet per minute, G99 F is inch per revolution, G76's P/Q/R words use the inch increment, the C-axis live-tool feed (`fm`) is per minute, and the diameter X word scales too. `tormach-lathe.cps` already does the equivalent for LinuxCNC and is the model.\n\nDone means: the post writes an inch program (G20 in the opening block, every length, per-rev feed, surface speed and G76 word in its inch unit, from the family's published manual), declares `programUnits = \"mm inch\"`, has inch goldens for its existing turning/thread/drill streams checked against the mm ones, and leaves every mm golden byte-identical.\n",
